      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose is well above the recommended maximum.\n\n- **Ordered:** 1600 mg four times daily, which is 6,400 mg/day.\n- **Maximum single dose:** 800 mg for prescription oral ibuprofen.\n- **Maximum daily dose:** 3,200 mg/day for adults. Over-the-counter use is limited to 1,200 mg/day.\n\nThis order is twice the maximum daily dose and twice the maximum single dose. Even with normal kidney and liver function, that raises the risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events.\n\nWhich of these did you mean?\n1. **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day). This is the usual maximum for inflammatory conditions.\n2. **600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day).\n3. **400 mg PO every 6 hours** for analgesia.\n4. **1600 mg/day total**, for example 400 mg four times daily or 800 mg twice daily.\n\nIf you do want 1600 mg four times daily, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording your confirmation and the clinical rationale. Otherwise, give me the dose you'd like and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
